knulli: rk3576 (Anbernic RG Vita Pro) on the Rockchip BSP 6.1

Applied after board/rockchip/rk3566/linux_bsp_patches (same repository and
commit): the RG Vita Pro device tree, the Synaptics DSX touchscreen driver
and Anbernic's singleadcjoy (sticks read from the MCU over SPI), which
replaces the SARADC variant of the rk3566 series in this build.  Two fixes
to Anbernic's driver, written for arm64's unsigned char while knulli builds
everything (the kernel too) with -fsigned-char: the SPI buffers and the LED
state are u8 (every MCU frame with a check byte >= 0x80 was rejected, so the
sticks never moved, and LED values above 127 went negative), led_level is
clamped to its 0..100 range, and a remove() drops the sysfs group (a reload
failed with -EEXIST).
